# Generated knowledge graph (issue #134)
# Rebuilt from the source beside it, and the tool rewrites the whole directory
# on every run — so tracking it made each regeneration a diff of hundreds of
# files with nothing in it, which is what buries the next real change.
graphify-out/

# Environment variables
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Uploads
uploads/

# SQLite database (dev)
mamen.db
mamen.db-shm
mamen.db-wal

# Seeded demo database (issue #139)
# Rebuilt from `packages/api/src/demo/dataset.ts` by `bun run seed:demo`, which
# is deterministic — so the file is output, and tracking a binary regenerated on
# demand only makes it something to keep in sync.
demo.db
demo.db-shm
demo.db-wal

# Bank statements (issue #108)
# A real export carries IBANs, counterparty names, amounts and payment
# references. One was tracked here for months under the bank's own download
# filename, so the repo root — where a download lands — is where this has to
# bite: no CSV belongs there, and fixtures live beside the parser that reads
# them. The named patterns catch the same file wherever else it is dropped,
# because the copy that mattered was not at the root but four directories down,
# named like a fixture. Synthetic fixtures under
# packages/web/src/features/import/__fixtures__/ are unaffected.
/*.csv
relev*_de_compte*.csv
*bank-statement*.csv

